  "notes": "Applies where the primary street setback is 1.5 m or greater (rule condition on C1.2.3). Frontage under 20 m: 1 small tree; 20 m or more: 1 small tree per 10 m of frontage, frontage rounded down to the nearest 10 m (note 2). Rows are listed from the largest band down so the first matching 'min' row wins; the last row catches frontages under 20 m. Frontages over 300 m fall in the 300 m row (30 trees) and need a manual count. The 'elsewhere on lot' column (1 small tree per dwelling, plantable in the street setback if room allows, note 1) is C1.2.3-r1. Tree provisions exclude ancillary dwellings. No tree provisions at R100-SL (Table 2.10a)."
}
